  "notes": "{志願|しがん}する emphasizes acting of one's own will, especially for difficult or important tasks.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive) / intransitive depending on use\n- Pattern: [task/role]に{志願|しがん}する or [task/role]を{志願|しがん}する\n\nFORMS:\n{志|し} (will, aspiration) + {願|がん} (wish, desire)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {志願|しがん}{兵|へい}: volunteer soldier\n- {志願|しがん}{者|しゃ}: volunteer, applicant\n- {自|みずか}ら{志願|しがん}する: to volunteer of one's own accord\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {応募|おうぼ}する: to apply (general, for jobs/contests)\n- {志願|しがん}する: to volunteer (emphasizes personal will, often for challenging roles)\n- ボランティアする: to volunteer (for community/charity work)",
